hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17366","Haddathana Yaqub, he said haddathana my father, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Akhbarani Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Amr ibn Awf, and he was an ally of Banu Amir ibn Luay, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah to al-Bahrayn to bring its tribute, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had made peace with the people of al-Bahrayn and appointed over them al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami. So Abu Ubaydah came with wealth from al-Bahrayn, so the Ansar heard of his coming and came to the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer he turned, so they faced him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled when he saw them and said: I think you have heard that Abu Ubaydah has come and brought something. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Rejoice and hope for what delights you, for by Allah it is not poverty I fear upon you, but I fear the world will be spread upon you as it was spread upon those before you, so you compete for it as they competed for it, and it distracts you as it distracted them."
"17367","Haddathana Sad, haddathani my father, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, he said akhbarani Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that Amr ibn Awf, and he was an ally of Banu Amir ibn Luay, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah, then he mentioned the like of it."
